title DRAFT v2: revoke -> remove -> HTML B -> guarded dispose -> guarded draw
autonumber
hide footbox
participant "Existing accept owner" as Session
control "ResultController" as Result
participant "Keyed HTML presenter" as HTML
participant "Revision-gated DOM adapter" as DOM
participant "Wheel renderer (value frames)" as Wheel
actor User
Session -> Result : accepted B + acceptanceSeq/cause/snapshot
Result -> DOM : revoke old instance/revision and native capabilities
Result -> DOM : remove imagery A
Result -> Result : full-B index, once policy / reconcile
Result -> HTML : publish B facts/source rows/summary, retained controls
alt retiring instance (replacement)
  Result -> Wheel : guarded synchronous dispose A, once
  alt dispose throw
    Wheel --> Result : retired failure
    Result -> Result : diagnostic; B remains published; continue
  end
else same instance, new revision
  Result -> Result : retain instance; prior revision already revoked
end
Result -> Wheel : update readonly B + fresh RevisionSink
note over DOM, Wheel
Leaf receives no live host/node or mutable currentHost.
Only closed, copied value frames and readonly numeric metrics.
Same-origin contract discipline, not a security sandbox.
end note
Wheel -> DOM : publish(frame, captured revision token)
DOM -> DOM : validate/copy frame; guard immediately before synchronous keyed patch
alt current token
  DOM -> DOM : patch B, retain live keyed controls; no await in write transaction
  DOM --> Wheel : committed
else revoked token, even before old promise settles
  DOM --> Wheel : revoked, no DOM write
end
alt current factory/update sync throw or async rejection
  Wheel --> Result : leaf failure, current token
  Result -> DOM : clear only wheel imagery
  Result -> HTML : visible local SVG warning; HTML B stays
  note over Session, Result
  Expected SVG leaf failure does not set requiresReconciliation or issue HTTP.
  Unexpected HTML/controller failure uses existing safe-read/fallback.
  end note
else stale async rejection
  Wheel --> Result : retired token + failure
  Result -> Result : diagnostic only; do not replace B warning/state
else current update completed with valid frame
  Wheel --> Result : completion
  Result -> Result : rendered current revision
end
User -> DOM : native canonical activation on live node
DOM -> DOM : current token + connected capability + canonical key
DOM -> Result : canonical intent
Result -> HTML : selection uses accepted B, keyed patch
Result -> DOM : selection frame, retain active point/row
note over Result, DOM
Planet activation does not focus()/scroll.
Frame patch/resize does not remount focused control.
Bounded run04 proves principle; full mounted integration NOT RUN.
end note
@enduml
